# Copy to .env and adjust if needed (.env is git-ignored). All values are optional.
API_PORT=8790
API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Relative paths resolve against the current working directory (pnpm runs scripts from apps/api).
DATABASE_PATH=data/diy-ai.sqlite
WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5190
# Scratch mode: `pnpm dev:scratch` / `pnpm start:scratch` (same as dev/start but with DIY_AI_SCRATCH=1) run the API
# against data-scratch/diy-ai.sqlite (created on demand, git-ignored) and ignore DATABASE_PATH; the main database is
# never opened. The startup line says "using SCRATCH database". Use it while migrations are being written.
# DIY_AI_SCRATCH=1
# Before applying pending migrations to an existing database the API writes a verified backup to
# <database dir>/backups/ (newest 10 kept). If that fails, it refuses to migrate and exits.
